WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:06.363
If Sperry was right, the target itself carries a cue.

2
00:00:07.303 --> 00:00:08.903
Can we ask an axon to read it?

3
00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:14.023
In 1987, Friedrich Bonhoeffer's group built a striped carpet.

4
00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:19.787
Membranes from the front and back of chick tectum lay in alternating narrow lanes.

5
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.830
A strip of retina lay across them, so each growing axon met border after border.

6
00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:29.323
Where will axons from the temporal retina grow?

7
00:00:35.317 --> 00:00:39.777
Temporal axons grew along the front lanes and stayed off the back ones.

8
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:42.057
Nasal axons grew on both.

9
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.590
On either membrane alone, both grew well.

10
00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.990
So the back membrane was not simply a poor surface.

11
00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.873
Now heat the back membranes first.

12
00:00:54.793 --> 00:00:56.253
What will the temporal axons do?

13
00:01:02.216 --> 00:01:03.556
The avoidance vanished.

14
00:01:04.436 --> 00:01:07.476
An attractant on the unheated front lanes would have kept it.

15
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.120
So the cue is a heat-sensitive repellent at the back of the tectum.

16
00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:20.410
In 1995, one paper found a repellent at the back of the tectum, now called

17
00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.650
ephrin-A5.

18
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:27.510
A second paper mapped the gradient of ephrin-A2, which had been cloned the year

19
00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:28.510
before.

20
00:01:28.933 --> 00:01:32.873
Ephrin-A rises from front to back across the tectum.

21
00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:37.553
Its receptor, EphA, runs the opposite way, high in temporal retina.

22
00:01:38.616 --> 00:01:41.056
Why does more receptor mean ending at the front?

23
00:01:42.016 --> 00:01:46.736
Take toy numbers. Repulsion is the receptor level times the local ligand.

24
00:01:47.716 --> 00:01:50.336
Each axon enters at the front and grows back.

25
00:01:51.196 --> 00:01:54.096
It keeps its branches where the repulsion reaches the limit.

26
00:01:55.116 --> 00:01:58.176
Three axons carry low, middle and high receptor.

27
00:01:59.036 --> 00:02:00.376
Which reaches the limit first?

28
00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:10.439
The axon with the most receptor hits the limit first, at the front edge.

29
00:02:11.279 --> 00:02:13.239
The axon with the least ends at the back.

30
00:02:17.183 --> 00:02:22.943
One correction. In chick and mouse, axons first overshoot their zone, then sprout

31
00:02:22.943 --> 00:02:23.943
side branches.

32
00:02:24.716 --> 00:02:29.396
Ephrin-A keeps branches from forming and surviving behind the right zone.

33
00:02:30.356 --> 00:02:32.296
The overshooting part is later removed.

34
00:02:33.349 --> 00:02:37.849
So where an axon stops means where it keeps its branches, its termination zone.

35
00:02:38.899 --> 00:02:41.319
The takeaway: more receptor, less ligand.

36
00:02:41.999 --> 00:02:45.179
In the toy, two opposite slopes put the axons in order.
